---
title: Login & Risk-Based Step-Up
---
%% Password sign-in and the three ways it can end: tokens, an enrolled-2FA challenge, or an
%% anomaly-driven step-up (FR-TPF-1). This is the flow that makes E2E login impossible with
%% ANOMALY_DETECTION_ENABLED=true — see e2e/README.md.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant SPA as Angular<br/>LoginComponent
    participant RL as RateLimitFilter<br/>@Order(-200)
    participant API as UserController
    participant AM as AuthenticationManager<br/>+ BCrypt
    participant RISK as LoginRiskService
    participant SESS as SessionService
    participant DB as MySQL

    U->>SPA: Enter email + password
    SPA->>RL: POST /user/login

    alt over 10 requests/min from this IP
        RL-->>SPA: 429 Too Many Requests
        note right of RL: Runs BEFORE Spring Security,<br/>so throttling costs no JWT parsing<br/>or database work.
    end

    RL->>API: forward
    API->>DB: countRecentFailuresByEmail(email, window)
    alt brute-force threshold exceeded
        API-->>SPA: 401 — generic failure message
    end

    API->>AM: authenticate(email, password)
    AM->>DB: loadUserByUsername → UserRepoImpl
    AM->>AM: BCrypt verify (strength 12)

    alt bad credentials OR unknown account
        AM-->>API: AuthenticationException
        API-->>SPA: 401 — one identical message for both cases
        note right of API: Never reveals whether the<br/>account exists.
    end

    API->>RISK: assess(user, device, clientIp)
    RISK->>DB: This account's own successful-login history
    note right of RISK: Compared only against the<br/>account's own past — never against<br/>other accounts, so a risk verdict<br/>can't become an oracle either.

    alt NEW_DEVICE and/or NEW_NETWORK
        RISK-->>API: risky
        API->>DB: Store one-time code
        API-->>SPA: 200 {user, stepUp: true} — no tokens
        note over API, SPA: Copy says an extra check was needed,<br/>never which signal fired.
        U->>SPA: Enter emailed code
        SPA->>API: GET /user/verify/code/{email}/{code}
    else enrolled 2FA (TOTP / SMS)
        API-->>SPA: 200 {user, isUsingMfa: true} — no tokens
        U->>SPA: Enter authenticator or SMS code
        SPA->>API: GET /user/verify/code/{email}/{code}
    else no risk, no 2FA
        note over API, SESS: Straight through
    end

    API->>SESS: issueTokenPair(principal, request)
    SESS->>DB: INSERT refreshsessions (new family + jti)
    SESS-->>API: access (30 min) + refresh (5 days)
    API-->>SPA: 200 {user, access_token, refresh_token}
    SPA->>SPA: Persist both to localStorage
    SPA->>U: Navigate to dashboard
